Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:41:23 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 01/23] rusticc: parity against the COSMOS reference, 149/150
 identical

- rusticc/tools/ref_setup.sh builds a COSMOS-style reference (~/rk/cosmos_ref:
  no git, klippy/.version, compiled, c_helper without FP contraction);
  case_cmp.sh runs the cases against it
- util.rs get_git_version: Kalico's logic (git describe, else klippy/.version)
- APP_NAME "Rusticc"
- python 3.15 tracebacks: ModuleNotFoundError "Did you mean" for kinematics
  (traceback.py / suggestions.c over importlib's discover order), json.dumps
  "when serializing ... item ..." notes on gcode_macro variable errors
- pyliteral: literal_eval builds dicts pair by pair (unhashable key message,
  repeated keys) and json errors follow the encoder's order; unit test of 33
  literals against CPython 3.15

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
